FINAL ANSWER:
Two people hold most of the code that is still here: Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson.

Figures are surviving lines at HEAD (`git blame -w -M -C`), 1,987 lines in 19 files.

| Author | Surviving lines | Share | Commits | Commit share |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses, merged) | 810 | 40.8% | 95 | 30.1% |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 629 | 31.7% | 143 | 45.3% |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | 4.8% | 2 | 0.6% |
| Jon Church | 72 | 3.6% | 3 | 0.9% |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | 3.4% | 2 | 0.6% |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | 2.6% | 3 | 0.9% |
| Ignacio Mangas | 44 | 2.2% | 2 | 0.6% |
| alex94puchades | 34 | 1.7% | 5 | 1.6% |
| Linus Unnebäck | 26 | 1.3% | 1 | 0.3% |
| Ollie Buck | 17 | 0.9% | 1 | 0.3% |

52 more authors hold the rest.

- **Commits vs. code:** Wilson has the most commits (143), but Goode has more code that survives. Much of Wilson's work has been rewritten or removed since.
- **Identity merge:** Troy Goode appears under two addresses. Counted separately, `<email redacted>` has 762 lines (38.3%) and `troy@laptop.example` has 48 lines (2.4%). The merge assumes both are the same person because the name matches. That is a guess from names and addresses, and I have not confirmed it. I merged it in memory only and did not write `.mailmap`.
- **Alex Puchades:** `alex94puchades` is probably also "Alejandro Caravaca Puchades", since both use `<email redacted>`. The tool did not merge them here. The 34 lines under `alex94puchades` are counted on their own, which is a possible undercount for that person.
- **Bus factor:**
  - **Definition:** the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines together reach 50% of the lines counted.
  - **Whole repository, merged:** 2 authors (Goode and Wilson, 72.4%), and 4 authors reach 80%.
  - **Unmerged:** 2 authors (70.0%), and 5 authors reach 80%.
- **Reformat commit:** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes") rewrote 1,016 lines across 4 files. It is listed in `.git-blame-ignore-revs`, so the figures leave it out and the original authors keep their lines.
- **Mechanical rewrites checked:** the tool examined the 143 commits that hold surviving lines. It set none aside beyond `62628c0`. It flagged 5 more as possibly mechanical, and all 5 are counted, not set aside:
  - `fcd2b56` (Goode, ESLint switch): 19 lines
  - `739dc11` (Wilson, license reformat): 17 lines
  - `00d6eec` (Wilson, yaml eslint config): 9 lines
  - `344ce1e` (Wilson, eslint bump): 1 line
  - `9c2b59d` (Wilson, eslint bump): 1 line

  I looked only at `fcd2b56`. It touched 10 test files, with 65 insertions and 98 deletions, and does look like a cleanup. Each of the 5 commits holds too few lines to change the ranking.
- **Left out:** one bot (10 lines, 11 commits) is excluded. The tool also drops lockfiles, generated files and vendored code, and merge commits are excluded from the commit counts. Both are the tool's defaults.
- **Copy detection:** figures use `-M -C`. The tool printed no note that copy detection moved anyone's share.

These counts show only which lines remain. They don't show code quality, review work, design done elsewhere, or code that was deleted on purpose.

